# DELVE — static web build (GitHub + Vercel; no engine).
#
# The game is `web/`: HTML, ES modules, JSON, PNG and OGG. Everything committed
# here is served straight from the repository, so this file only excludes
# scratch, tooling caches and regenerable QA output.

# --- tooling -----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.vercel/
.venv/
venv/

# --- scratch -----------------------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.tmp
deliverables/

# --- generated previews ------------------------------------------------
# `tools/preview_screen.py` renders the pages to PNG so a layout can be checked
# without a browser; the sheets are regenerable, so they stay out of Git. The
# text atlas in `tools/atlas/` is not preview output: the offline renderers draw
# their text from it, so it ships and is checked by `check_project.py`.
web/preview/
tools/__pycache__/
